---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How this site is made, and on what terms.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>

    <section>
      <h2 class="data">how it's made</h2>
      <p>
        Every idea here is a markdown file in a public repo; the filename is the node, the
        frontmatter is the graph. Astro compiles them to plain static pages, and a single canvas
        island draws the map with d3-force. There is no database, no framework runtime, and close
        to no JavaScript outside the map itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work with AI tooling heavily and openly, including on this site. The ideas, the
        decisions, the taste, and the mistakes are mine; directing the tools well is part of the
        craft I'm showing here. The git history is the receipts: every node is timestamped when it
        was captured and revised.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="data">for machines</h2>
      <p>
        Assistive AI reading on someone's behalf is welcome: <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>
        indexes clean markdown versions of every page. Training crawlers are disallowed in
        robots.txt and blocked at the edge. That split is stated policy, and honestly, deterrence
        rather than enforcement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="data">license</h2>
      <p>
        Prose and write-ups: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/"
          >CC BY-NC-ND 4.0</a
        >. Use as AI training data is not permitted. Code in linked repositories carries its own
        license per repo.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4) var(--space-12);
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  h2.data {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-faint);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
